    "https://msmu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203810": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, PsyD Program",
      "description": "Mount Saint Mary's University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Faculty, PsyD Program Mount Saint Mary's University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Faculty, PsyD Program Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Faculty, PsyD Program Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Psychology Locations: Los Angeles, CA Posted: Aug 17, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Salary Type: Annually Position ID: 203810 Share Job Description: The PsyD Clinical Psychology program at Mount Saint Mary's University (Los Angeles) invites applicants with a doctoral degree (PhD or PsyD) in Psychology for teaching as an adjunct in our APA Accredited PsyD in Clinical Psychology program. The PsyD in Clinical Health Psychology is designed to prepare graduates to be practicing Psychologists in the public and private sectors. There are two emphases within the PsyD program:  Latinx Mental Health and Diverse Populations. Responsibilities: Primary responsibilities include teaching doctoral-level courses in clinical psychology, specifically courses that address both the applied and scientific foundations of psychology. Facilitate Classroom. Our institution uses Canvas for homework submission, attendance, files. Manage the online grading system and utilize current technology in the performance of job duties Utilize a variety of teaching tools and teaching modalities to guide students through their studies using active collaboration and active learning techniques Course and syllabus preparation Assessment and evaluation of learners Holding office hours and meeting with students Abide by all relevant university and/or department procedures and policies Skills: Proficient computer skills, including proficiency with Microsoft Office programs. The ability to work independently and be self-motivated. High level of accuracy and attention to detail and the ability to problem solve. The ability to explain complex requirements in clear and concise terms. The ability to be flexible with workflow to meet the needs of the department and students and to manage multiple tasks per required deadlines. The drive to encourage, direct, hold accountable and guide candidates toward task completion. Must demonstrate the ability to work as an effective team member. Culturally humble and ability to communicate and interact effectively with diverse people. Ability to exercise discretion and tact in all interpersonal interactions, and to maintain confidentiality. Collaboration and partnering with other university stakeholders to support candidate success. Ability to make administrative/procedural decisions and judgments. Position salary: $2,283.15 per unit Requirements: Applicants must have a doctoral degree in Clinical, Counseling or closely related field in psychology, have attended an APA Accredited doctoral program, and be eligible for licensure as a Psychologist in the State of California. Applicants will have experience teaching in a clinical training program or undergraduate courses related to psychology. This candidate will demonstrate successful doctoral teaching. Additional Information: Work Location : Doheny Campus (Downtown Los Angeles) Start Date: August 24, 2026 Applications Deadline: Open until filled Application Instructions: To Apply : Interested applicants should submit: A cover letter describing the applicant's fit with the specific position and university pillars of teaching Curriculum vitae or resume (un)official transcripts Optional: Teaching accomplishments (examples include: course syllabus, course materials, course plans, teaching evaluations, etc.) Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questions: Please contact Dr. Esmeralda Zamudio, Department of Psychology, ezamudio@msmu.edu or psydclinicalpsychology@msmu.edu Applicants must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the United States. The University will not assist applicants with any visa matters. A background check will be required. Employees may disclose their COVID-19 vaccination status with MSMU's Human Resources on a voluntary basis. Some MSMU clinical healthcare partners may require proof of COVID-19 vaccination to work at their facilities. If required, your academic division will inform you. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Chalon Campus, WEST LA 12001 Chalon Road Los Angeles, CA 90049 Doheny Campus, DOWNTOWN LA 10 Chester Place Los Angeles, CA 90007"
    },
    "https://msmu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=127480": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Traditional Undergraduate Program, Psychology Department",
      "description": "Mount Saint Mary's University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Faculty, Traditional Undergraduate Program, Psychology Department Mount Saint Mary's University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Faculty, Traditional Undergraduate Program, Psychology Department Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Faculty, Traditional Undergraduate Program, Psychology Department Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Department of Psychology Locations: Los Angeles, CA Posted: Jan 11, 2021 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 127480 Share Job Description: The Psychology Department: The Psychology Department at Mount Saint Mary's University, Los Angeles, offers Baccalaureate, Master's and Doctoral degrees across two campuses. One campus, Chalon, is on the Westside of Los Angeles while Doheny is near downtown Los Angeles. This opportunity is within the TUG program, which teaches primarily traditionally college-age women in a traditional M-F, 8 am - 9 pm format. Most classes are in-person on one of our two campuses in Los Angeles. The TUG psychology program seeks to attract and retain highly qualified faculty that share the University's and program's values. General Responsibilities Because Mount Saint Mary's Psychology Department is committed to helping students achieve success with us and in their careers, we seek adjunct faculty members who are scholars as well as scholar-practitioners. The adjunct faculty member shall be responsible for the following: Teach assigned classes under the supervision of the Psychology Department Chair and TUG Program Director; Create a syllabus and course timeline for students each semester and post it online before class starts. Help students fulfill their maximum potential in mastering course content; Actively engage students through frequent interaction that motivates them to succeed and conveys a genuine energy and enthusiasm for their learning. Guide students through their studies using active collaboration and active learning techniques. Provide rich and regular constructive feedback, utilize rubrics effectively to assess student learning outcomes, and acknowledge student accomplishments. Manage the online grading system weekly and utilize current technology in the performance of job duties; Submit grades in a timely fashion; Maintain a thorough and up-to-date subject-matter expertise in regular teaching field; Maintain standards of professional conduct and ethics appropriate to the professional position; Abide by all relevant university and/or department procedures and policies. The above statements describe the job's essential responsibilities and requirements. They are not an exhaustive list of the duties that may be assigned to successful applicants. Requirements: Qualifications Successful candidates should possess a Master's degree or Doctoral degree in psychology, counseling, or a closely related field. The candidate will be able to teach undergraduate courses related to psychology. The candidate will be able to integrate technology into the teaching and learning process. The candidate will be able to professionally interact with students, other educators, educational institution representatives, and the public. Application Instructions: Please complete the online application and submit the following documents: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae - Your most recently updated CV Teaching accomplishments (examples include: course syllabus, course materials, course plans, teaching evaluations, etc.) (Un)official transcripts Applicants must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the United States. The University will not assist applicants with any visa matters. A background check will be required. Employees may disclose their COVID-19 vaccination status with MSMU's Human Resources on a voluntary basis. Some MSMU clinical healthcare partners may require proof of COVID-19 vaccination to work at their facilities. If required, your academic division will inform you. URL: www.msmu.edu/undergraduate-bachelor-programs/psychology/ Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Chalon Campus, WEST LA 12001 Chalon Road Los Angeles, CA 90049 Doheny Campus, DOWNTOWN LA 10 Chester Place Los Angeles, CA 90007"
    },
    "https://msmu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=199582": {
      "title": "Adjunct Laboratory Instructor, General & Organic Chemistry, Physical Sciences/Math Department",
      "description": "Mount Saint Mary's University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Laboratory Instructor, General & Organic Chemistry, Physical Sciences/Math Department Mount Saint Mary's University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Laboratory Instructor, General & Organic Chemistry, Physical Sciences/Math Department Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Laboratory Instructor, General & Organic Chemistry, Physical Sciences/Math Department Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Physical Sciences Locations: Los Angeles, CA Posted: Apr 16, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 199582 Share Job Description: The Department of Physical Sciences at Mount Saint Mary's University (Los Angeles) invites applications for an Adjunct Laboratory Instructors to teach General Chemistry and/or Organic Chemistry laboratory courses. We seek instructors who are committed to hands-on learning, laboratory safety, and high-quality undergraduate instruction. About the Opportunity MSMU's General and Organic Chemistry labs are core requirements for students majoring in Chemistry, Biochemistry, and Biology. All laboratory sections meet in person at the University's Chalon Campus on the Westside of Los Angeles. Our program uses a standardized curriculum and syllabus to ensure consistency and fairness across all sections. Course materials and laboratory experimental procedures will be provided to guarantee foundational laboratory skills essential for success in higher-level coursework are understood.  Each lab section meets for 4 hours, including a pre-lab lecture to prepare students for the day's experiment. Compensation $2,283.15 per teaching unit Each laboratory section = 3 teaching units Up to 9 units per semester Responsibilities Teaching & Course Delivery Teach assigned laboratory sections under the supervision of the Department Chair. Update and post the provided syllabus template and course timeline each semester. Maintain alignment with the shared curriculum and weekly lab schedule. Create an engaging, student-centered learning environment that supports both conceptual understanding and experimental technique. Student Engagement & Assessment Provide timely, constructive, rubric-based lab report feedback. Maintain accurate, up-to-date grades in the LMS. Submit final grades on time and issue student success alerts when appropriate. If possible, attend the annual departmental assessment meeting and provide written data and feedback when teaching assessed courses. Laboratory Safety Instructors must \"model and enforce all institutional, departmental, and discipline-standard laboratory safety regulations at all times.\" Expectations include: Delivering safety briefings at the start of each class. Ensuring proper PPE use (goggles, lab coats, gloves, etc.). Monitoring technique and correcting unsafe behavior immediately. Maintaining proper chemical storage, labeling, and housekeeping. Following emergency protocols and reporting all accidents, exposures, or near-misses promptly. Collaborating with the Laboratory Coordinator and Department Chair to strengthen safety culture. Professional Expectations Communicate regularly with the Department Chair and Laboratory Coordinator. Maintain current subject-matter expertise and best practices in laboratory instruction. Uphold professional conduct, ethics, and all University policies. Coordinate instructional needs with the Laboratory Coordinator (lab setup and breakdown are handled by staff). Requirements: Minimum Qualifications Candidates must have: A Master's degree, Doctoral degree, or doctoral candidacy in Chemistry, Biochemistry, or a related field. Ability to teach undergraduate General and/or Organic Chemistry laboratory courses. Commitment to following the common laboratory curriculum and schedule. Experience using instructional technologies (e.g., LMS). Strong professional communication skills and commitment to laboratory safety. Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis. Please complete the online application and submit the following documents: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching accomplishments (e.g., syllabus, course materials, evaluations) (Un)official transcripts All materials should be sent via Interview Exchange Questions may be directed to the MSMU Physical Sciences Department at kliu@msmu.edu. Applicants must provide proof of eligibility to work in the United States. The University does not sponsor visas. A background check is required. Employees may disclose their COVID-19 vaccination status with MSMU's Human Resources on a voluntary basis. Some MSMU clinical healthcare partners may require proof of COVID-19 vaccination to work at their facilities. If required, your academic division will inform you. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Chalon Campus, WEST LA 12001 Chalon Road Los Angeles, CA 90049 Doheny Campus, DOWNTOWN LA 10 Chester Place Los Angeles, CA 90007"
    },
    "https://msmu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=202210": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Chemistry (Tenure-Track, 9-month)",
      "description": "Mount Saint Mary's University\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Chemistry (Tenure-Track, 9-month) Mount Saint Mary's University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Chemistry (Tenure-Track, 9-month) Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Chemistry (Tenure-Track, 9-month) Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Physical Sciences Locations: Los Angeles, CA Posted: Jul 6, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Position ID: 202210 Share Job Description: Mount Saint Mary's University invites applications for a tenure-track position in Chemistry at the Assistant Professor level, beginning Fall 2027. We seek a collaborative educator-scholar with expertise in chemical instrumentation who is committed to excellence in undergraduate teaching, mentoring, and inclusive pedagogy, and to the development of a sustained undergraduate research program. The successful candidate will contribute to a department focused on student-centered learning, hands-on scientific training, and equitable access to research opportunities, particularly for students from historically underrepresented backgrounds. Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate courses in general, organic, analytical, and/or physical chemistry, including laboratories Develop, maintain, and actively use shared instrumentation resources in both teaching and research Establish a productive and externally funded undergraduate research program, mentoring and involving students in independent and course-based research Contribute to curriculum development, program assessment, student advisement and departmental initiatives Engage in service to the department, university, and broader community Participate in faculty development opportunities and attend conferences Position Annual Hiring Salary Range: $73,450 - $76,350 Hiring salary can be above the posted pay range if candidate's qualifications are determined to be above the minimum requirements of the position description. Requirements: Ph.D. in Chemistry or a closely related field (completed by start date) Demonstrated expertise with chemical instrumentation Strong commitment to undergraduate teaching and mentoring Clear ability and commitment to developing and sustaining an undergraduate research program Commitment to working effectively with diverse student populations in an inclusive learning environment Preferred Qualifications Experience maintaining, troubleshooting, or managing instrumentation Experience mentoring undergraduate students in research Demonstrated commitment to equity, inclusion, and student success in STEM Experience in resource-conscious research program design Additional Information: Work Location : Chalon Campus (West Los Angeles) Start Date: August 19, 2027 Applications Deadline: Open until filled Application Instructions: To Apply : Interested applicants should submit: Cover letter addressing interest in MSMU's mission Curriculum vitae Teaching statement Research statement Contact information for references Applicants must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the United States. The University will not assist applicants with any visa matters. A background check will be required. Employees may disclose their COVID-19 vaccination status with MSMU's Human Resources on a voluntary basis. Some MSMU clinical healthcare partners may require proof of COVID-19 vaccination to work at their facilities. If required, your academic division will inform you. Review of applications will begin on October 15, 2026. Applications received by this date will receive full consideration; however, the position will remain open until November 30, 2026 or until filled. Questions: Please contact Dr. Sylvine Deprele, Department Chair of Physical Sciences, sdeprele@msmu.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Chalon Campus, WEST LA 12001 Chalon Road Los Angeles, CA 90049 Doheny Campus, DOWNTOWN LA 10 Chester Place Los Angeles, CA 90007"
    },
    "https://msmu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=198950": {
      "title": "Director of the Traditional BSN (TBSN) Program and Full time, Tenure-track faculty position",
      "description": "Mount Saint Mary's University\nJob Posting: Director of the Traditional BSN (TBSN) Program and Full time, Tenure-track faculty position Mount Saint Mary's University \n\tJob Posting: Director of the Traditional BSN (TBSN) Program and Full time, Tenure-track faculty position Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Director of the Traditional BSN (TBSN) Program and Full time, Tenure-track faculty position Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Nursing Locations: Los Angeles, CA Posted: Apr 3, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Position ID: 198950 Share Job Description: Mount Saint Mary's University-Los Angeles invites applications for the Director of the Traditional BSN (TBSN) Program.  This administrative position is also a 12 month full-time, tenure-track faculty position at the rank of assistant, associate, or full professor.  The Director of the Traditional BSN (TBSN) Program provides strategic leadership, operational oversight, and student-centered guidance under the direction of the Dean of Nursing. This role oversees program operations, admissions, curriculum implementation, and faculty support while fostering an exceptional advisement and student experience. The Director serves as a key liaison across university departments and external partners and maintains strong working relationships to support student success and program excellence.  Three assistant directors support the director in administering the program. As part of a university founded by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, the TBSN Director is expected to embody and advance the CSJ charism -- service to the dear neighbor without distinction, commitment to justice, compassion, and inclusive community. This includes fostering a learning environment grounded in dignity, equity, and holistic care for students, faculty, and the communities we serve. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Manages TBSN's program admissions processes. Provides leadership related to program curriculum and evaluation. Provides faculty support and guidance related to student issues. Provides overarching student support related to academics, psychological, social and emotional needs and safety. Notifies Dean and contacts university departments as appropriate. Supervises and assumes responsibility for program operations Ongoing advisement, monitoring, and advocacy of students within the nursing department, university and community. Represents the BSN Program through engagement with professional organizations. Maintains faculty responsibility by serving on nursing and University committee(s) Teaches approximately 6 credit hours per year. Participates in academic advisement activities. Rank and Salary This is a tenure-track Assistant, Associate Professor or Professor position, depending on qualifications. Salary is commensurate with education, experience, and scholarly accomplishments. Tenure expectations follow University policy and include excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. Position Annual Hiring Salary Range: $120,000 - $150,000 (dependent on rank and qualifications) Hiring salary can be above the posted pay range if candidate's qualifications are determined to be above the minimum requirements of the position description. Requirements: Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong knowledge of BSN curriculum, academic advisement, admissions processes, program evaluation, BRN and accreditation regulations, and budget management. Ability to manage multiple priorities, meet deadlines, and develop effective plans. Strong communication skills with students, faculty, staff, and external partners. Ability to collaborate effectively across departments and organizations. Skilled in data collection, analysis, and interpretation. Demonstrated leadership, sound judgment, and decision-making abilities. Ability to deliver presentations to large groups. Education: (established by the California Board of Registered Nursing, 1425a) Master's or higher degree from an accredited college or university, which includes course work in nursing, education, or administration. Doctoral degree preferred. Experience: A minimum of one year's experience in an administrative position with validated performance of administrative responsibilities (described in BRN regulation 1420h) A minimum of two years of experience teaching in a pre-licensure registered (RN) nursing program At least one year of continuous experience as a registered nurse providing direct patient care and/or equivalent experience as determined by the Board Licenses and Certifications: Eligible for RN license in the state of California Other Requirements: Background check required by policy. Additional Information: Work Location : Chalon Campus (West LA) with periodic visits to the Doheny campus (Downtown LA) Start Date: July 1, 2026 or sooner Applications Deadline: Open until filled Mount Saint Mary's University is committed to fostering an inclusive, mission-driven academic community that prepares compassionate, ethical nurse leaders. The University encourages applications from individuals who are dedicated to advancing equity, community engagement, and the charism of the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet. Application Instructions: To Apply : Interested applicants should submit: A cover letter describing the applicant's fit with the specific position and university pillars of teaching Curriculum vitae or resume Teaching statement Course evaluations (un)official transcripts Two letters of reference via the Interview Exchange link below Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applicants must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the United States. The University will not assist applicants with any visa matters. A background check will be required. Employees may disclose their COVID-19 vaccination status with MSMU's Human Resources on a voluntary basis. Some MSMU clinical healthcare partners may require proof of COVID-19 vaccination to work at their facilities. If required, your academic division will inform you. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Chalon Campus, WEST LA 12001 Chalon Road Los Angeles, CA 90049 Doheny Campus, DOWNTOWN LA 10 Chester Place Los Angeles, CA 90007"
    },
    "https://msmu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=198943": {
      "title": "Fletcher Jones Chair of Nursing, Full-time, Tenure-track faculty position",
      "description": "Mount Saint Mary's University\nJob Posting: Fletcher Jones Chair of Nursing, Full-time, Tenure-track faculty position Mount Saint Mary's University \n\tJob Posting: Fletcher Jones Chair of Nursing, Full-time, Tenure-track faculty position Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Fletcher Jones Chair of Nursing, Full-time, Tenure-track faculty position Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Nursing Locations: Los Angeles, CA Posted: Apr 3, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Position ID: 198943 Share Job Description: Mount Saint Mary's University-Los Angeles invites applications for the Fletcher Jones Chair of Nursing, a 9 month full-time, tenure-track faculty position at the rank of assistant, associate, or full professor reporting to the Dean of Nursing. This endowed role provides a unique opportunity to shape the future of community health nursing in Los Angeles by building meaningful partnerships, advancing service-learning, and supporting faculty and student scholarship in diverse communities. The Fletcher Jones Chair will work collaboratively across all MSMU nursing programs to strengthen community health curricula, expand student learning opportunities, and elevate the University's visibility and impact in community-based health initiatives. Supervisory Responsibility No staff or student employee responsibility Will supervise nursing students in the community setting. Position Responsibilities Develop, coordinate, and supervise ongoing community-based service-learning opportunities for nursing students in traditional and non-traditional healthcare settings. Build and sustain partnerships with community and community-based health organizations serving linguistically and culturally diverse populations. Collaborate with faculty and other MSMU departments to integrate community health content and service-learning across the curriculum. Work with the clinical placement team to establish and maintain agency affiliations. Provide continuing education offerings for the external nursing community. Seek grant opportunities that support service-learning and community engagement. Disseminate program outcomes through presentations, publications, and professional engagement. Conduct or participate in research and scholarly writing; support faculty scholarship. Fulfill faculty responsibilities as outlined in the MSMU Faculty Handbook, including teaching 15 units per academic year (this includes a six credit hour release for endowed chair activities) Supervise nursing students in community settings. Evening or weekend work may be required. The Fletcher Jones Endowed Chair also has access to a small budget to support the above activities. Rank and Salary This is a tenure-track Assistant, Associate Professor or Professor position, depending on qualifications. Salary is commensurate with education, experience, and scholarly accomplishments. Tenure expectations follow University policy and include excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. Position Annual Hiring Salary Range: $90,000 - $120,000 (dependent on rank and qualifications) Hiring salary can be above the posted pay range if candidate's qualifications are determined to be above the minimum requirements of the position description. Requirements: Skills & Abilities Flexible work locations and scheduling. Strong collaborative and creative approach to problem-solving. Ability to work effectively with diverse populations. Demonstrated success working within teams. Knowledge Knowledge of the major research traditions. Knowledge of evidence-based practice. Education An earned doctoral degree in nursing or a closely related profession from an accredited university and a Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) required. Experience Five years of registered nurse experience. Two years of work in public or community health. Two years teaching in pre- and/or post-licensure nursing programs. One year providing direct patient care. One year of managerial experience. Grant application and management experience (preferred). Other California registered nurse license or eligibility to obtain one. Demonstrated record of publications and/or professional presentations. Additional Information: Work Location : Doheny Campus (Downtown Los Angeles) AND periodically the Chalon Campus (West LA) Start Date: August 19, 2026 Applications Deadline: Open until filled Mount Saint Mary's University is committed to fostering an inclusive, mission-driven academic community that prepares compassionate, ethical nurse leaders. The University encourages applications from individuals who are dedicated to advancing equity, community engagement, and the charism of the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet. Application Instructions: To Apply : Interested applicants should submit: A cover letter describing the applicant's fit with the specific position and university pillars of teaching Curriculum vitae or resume Teaching statement Course evaluations (un)official transcripts Two letters of reference via the Interview Exchange link below Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applicants must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the United States. The University will not assist applicants with any visa matters. A background check will be required. Employees may disclose their COVID-19 vaccination status with MSMU's Human Resources on a voluntary basis. Some MSMU clinical healthcare partners may require proof of COVID-19 vaccination to work at their facilities. If required, your academic division will inform you. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Chalon Campus, WEST LA 12001 Chalon Road Los Angeles, CA 90049 Doheny Campus, DOWNTOWN LA 10 Chester Place Los Angeles, CA 90007"
    },
    "https://msmu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=198009": {
      "title": "Full-Time Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing, Tenure-Track Position",
      "description": "Mount Saint Mary's University\nJob Posting: Full-Time Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing, Tenure-Track Position Mount Saint Mary's University \n\tJob Posting: Full-Time Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing, Tenure-Track Position Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Full-Time Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing, Tenure-Track Position Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Nursing Locations: Los Angeles, CA Posted: Mar 12, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Position ID: 198009 Share Job Description: Mount Saint Mary's University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing. As a University founded by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, we seek faculty who are committed to academic excellence, compassionate leadership, and service to the \"dear neighbor\" without distinction. The ideal candidate is a collaborative educator who brings a deep commitment to equity, student success, and the advancement of nursing practice. Faculty at Mount Saint Mary's are part of a vibrant, mission-driven community that values inclusive pedagogy, holistic student development, and the preparation of nurses who lead with courage, integrity, humility, and purpose. Primary Responsibilities Teaching Teach didactic, clinical, simulation, and/or laboratory courses. Teaching assignments are based on area of expertise. Create learning environments that reflect MSMU's commitment to inclusive excellence, social justice, and culturally humble nursing practice. Use evidence-based, student-centered teaching strategies that support diverse learners and reduce cognitive overload. Advisement Provide academic advisement, mentorship, and compassionate student support that reflects the CSJ spirit of gentleness, empathy, and encouragement. Scholarship Establish and or maintain an emerging program of scholarly inquiry consistent with Boyer's model of scholarship and AACN recommendations for Academic Nursing Scholarship. Service Contribute to departmental, college, and university committees, including curriculum development, assessment, and accreditation. Participate in professional organizations and maintain active engagement in the nursing profession. Support mission-driven initiatives that promote unity, reconciliation, and service to the dear neighbor, both within the University and in the broader community. Rank and Salary This is a tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor position. Salary is commensurate with education, experience, and scholarly accomplishments. Tenure expectations follow University policy and include excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. Position Annual Hiring Salary Range: $80,791 - $95,000 (dependent on rank and qualifications) Hiring salary can be above the posted pay range if candidate's qualifications are determined to be above the minimum requirements of the position description. Requirements: Required Qualifications Doctoral degree in Nursing (PhD, DNP, EdD) or related field; ABD considered with evidence of timely completion. Unencumbered RN license in California or eligibility for licensure. Demonstrated expertise in a clinical specialty area. Evidence of effective teaching in academic or clinical settings. Demonstrated potential for scholarly productivity. Preferred Qualifications Experience with curriculum design, assessment, and accreditation processes. Experience teaching in multiple modalities (in-person, hybrid, online). Certification in specialty practice or nursing education (e.g., CNE). Experience with simulation, virtual reality, or innovative teaching technologies. Professional Expectations Embody the Mount's core values of compassion, integrity, leadership, and service. Demonstrate cultural humility and the ability to teach and mentor a diverse student population. Maintain clinical competence and professional engagement. Contribute to a collaborative, supportive academic community grounded in the CSJ tradition of serving the dear neighbor without distinction. Additional Information: Work Location : Doheny Campus (Downtown Los Angeles) AND the Chalon Campus (West LA) Start Date: August 19, 2026 Applications Deadline: Open until filled Application Instructions: To Apply : Interested applicants should submit: A cover letter describing the applicant's fit with the specific position and university pillars of teaching Curriculum vitae or resume Teaching statement Course evaluations (un)official transcripts Two letters of reference via the Interview Exchange link below Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applicants must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the United States. The University will not assist applicants with any visa matters. A background check will be required. Employees may disclose their COVID-19 vaccination status with MSMU's Human Resources on a voluntary basis. Some MSMU clinical healthcare partners may require proof of COVID-19 vaccination to work at their facilities. If required, your academic division will inform you. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Chalon Campus, WEST LA 12001 Chalon Road Los Angeles, CA 90049 Doheny Campus, DOWNTOWN LA 10 Chester Place Los Angeles, CA 90007"
    },
    "https://msmu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203258": {
      "title": "Full-time Faculty and Assistant Director of Clinical Training, PsyD Program",
      "description": "Mount Saint Mary's University\nJob Posting: Full-time Faculty and Assistant Director of Clinical Training, PsyD Program Mount Saint Mary's University \n\tJob Posting: Full-time Faculty and Assistant Director of Clinical Training, PsyD Program Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Full-time Faculty and Assistant Director of Clinical Training, PsyD Program Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: Los Angeles, CA Posted: Jul 31, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 203258 Share Job Description: The Psychology Department at Mount Saint Mary's University (Los Angeles) invites applicants with a doctoral degree in Clinical or Counseling Psychology, for a full-time, 12-month faculty position in our APA Accredited PsyD in Clinical Psychology program, starting August 2027. The successful candidate for this position will demonstrate outstanding commitment to teaching diverse students from traditionally underserved populations, experience teaching graduate students in a clinical training program, as well as familiarity with APA Accreditation.  Our program was recently awarded APA Accreditation (on contingency) and will plan to apply for full Accreditation within two years. This is a \"contractually limited term\" appointment, which is a non-tenure-track appointment with annual contracts that can be renewed each year. About the University: Mount Saint Mary's University (www.msmu.edu) is a liberal arts university primarily for women. Founded in 1925 by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet in the Catholic intellectual tradition, the Mount is an institution dedicated to providing an excellent education directed toward leadership and service. Mount Saint Mary's University lives out its mission on two campuses: one in downtown Los Angeles (where the graduate program is located) and the second in the Brentwood area of Los Angeles. The university prides itself on maintaining a highly diverse student body, small classes, and a close working relationship between students and faculty. The Students: The Mount Saint Mary's University focus on social justice and community involvement attracts many first-generation college students from diverse socioeconomic backgrounds. The university encourages multicultural awareness throughout both academic and co-curricular activities. The Department: Mount Saint Mary's psychology program currently offers a baccalaureate and a master's degree, and launched the PsyD program fall 2019. The curriculum for the undergraduate psychology major has specializations in counseling/clinical, child/adolescent, research, and (general) applied psychology. The undergraduate program focuses on critical thinking, application, and preparation for continued education. The Master of Science degree in counseling psychology has two specializations. One fulfills the academic requirements for licensure in Marriage and Family Therapy in California; the second is in General Counseling Psychology. Bilingual (Spanish/English) speaking MFT students also have the option to obtain a certificate specializing in working with Spanish speaking populations. The PsyD in Clinical Health Psychology is designed to prepare graduates to be practicing Psychologists in the public and private sectors by training the next generation of ethical and socially-just health service psychologists who strive for cultural humility while integrating the practice and science of psychological services. There are two emphases within the PsyD program:  Latinx Mental Health and Diverse Populations. Position Annual Hiring Salary Range: $$92,000 - $105,000 Hiring salary can be above the posted pay range if candidate's qualifications are determined to be above the minimum requirements of the position description. Faculty Responsibilities: Responsibilities include teaching doctoral-level courses in clinical psychology, specifically courses that address both the applied and scientific foundations of psychology. Additional duties include ongoing program development, ongoing APA accreditation, and chairing dissertations. Other faculty responsibilities include advising and mentoring graduate students, scholarship/research, and participation in department and university service. Assistant Director of Clinical Training Responsibilities: Responsibilities include conducting and assisting site visits, assisting the DCT in managing the relationships between training sites and students. ADCT helps students prepare for interviews, provides advisement on clinical placements, advocates for students, and navigates student issues at clinical sites. The ADCT assists the DCT in implementing policies and with the integrity of the training program. The ADCT will also need to attend required practicum organization regularly scheduled meetings. Works collaboratively with the DCT to ensure quality clinical training is provided to the students. Requirements: Qualifications: Applicants must have a doctoral degree in counseling/clinical psychology from an APA Accredited doctoral program and be licensed as a Psychologist in the State of California (or be license eligible).  Applicants will have experience teaching in a clinical training program as well as familiarity with the APA accreditation process. Other Preferred Qualifications: Mount Saint Mary's has been designated as a Hispanic Serving Institution and has the special Carnegie Classification of \"Higher Access, Higher Opportunity.\"  As a university founded by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet with a charism of \"unifying love\", Mount Saint Mary's values and strives to create a welcoming environment with broad access and commitment to student success.  We seek applicants who can contribute to the well-being of the university community through participation, open communication, and dialogue and who can demonstrate their ability to teach and mentor in a diverse educational environment.  An appreciation of the liberal arts tradition of education and a commitment to serve the needs of both the campus, local, and professional community are desired.  We prefer candidates who can demonstrate successful doctoral teaching and dissertation research mentorship as well as a plan for research productivity at the time of appointment. Application Instructions: Application Procedure: Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Send vita, cover letter describing the applicant's fit with the specific position and university pillars of teaching, teaching statement, course evaluations, (un)official transcripts, and two letters of reference. Questions: Please contact Dr. Esmeralda Zamudio, PsyD Program Director, ezamudio@msmu.edu Applicants must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the United States. The University will not assist applicants with any visa matters. A background check will be required. Employees may disclose their COVID-19 vaccination status with MSMU's Human Resources on a voluntary basis. Some MSMU clinical healthcare partners may require proof of COVID-19 vaccination to work at their facilities. If required, your academic division will inform you. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Chalon Campus, WEST LA 12001 Chalon Road Los Angeles, CA 90049 Doheny Campus, DOWNTOWN LA 10 Chester Place Los Angeles, CA 90007"
    },
    "https://msmu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=198313": {
      "title": "Full-Time Faculty, Graduate Master's in Counseling Psychology, Contractually Limited Term",
      "description": "Mount Saint Mary's University\nJob Posting: Full-Time Faculty, Graduate Master's in Counseling Psychology, Contractually Limited Term Mount Saint Mary's University \n\tJob Posting: Full-Time Faculty, Graduate Master's in Counseling Psychology, Contractually Limited Term Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Full-Time Faculty, Graduate Master's in Counseling Psychology, Contractually Limited Term Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Psychology Locations: Los Angeles, CA Posted: Mar 19, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Position ID: 198313 Share Job Description: Mount Saint Mary's University invites applications for a full-time Contractually Limited Term (CLT), 9-month academic-year faculty appointment with assigned time to serve as Clinical Coordinator for the Master of Science in Counseling Psychology, Marriage and Family Therapy (MFT) hybrid track. The Clinical Coordinator provides leadership for the practicum and clinical training components of the program. This role oversees student placements, ensures compliance with California Board of Behavioral Sciences (BBS) regulations and applicable accreditation standards, and serves as the primary liaison among students, faculty, clinical sites, and university offices. This is a non-tenure line position. The appointment is one year in length and may be renewed annually contingent upon successful fulfillment of faculty responsibilities. After five successful contract years, the faculty member's contract may be renewed for up to five additional years. Contracts may be renewed continually for up to five years during the final year of each term. Faculty members in CLT positions are eligible to apply for promotion in rank (Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Professor). Essential Duties and Responsibilities Clinical Coordination (Primary Responsibility) Oversee all aspects of student clinical placements in the hybrid MFT program. Develop, vet, and maintain practicum sites consistent with BBS and program standards. Serve as liaison among the University, students, clinical supervisors, community partners, and administrative offices. Monitor student eligibility, readiness, and clinical hour progression to ensure regulatory compliance. Lead pre-practicum orientations, informational meetings, and workshops regarding placement requirements, documentation standards, ethical practice, and licensure pathways. Provide leadership, training, and oversight for practicum course instructors to ensure alignment with BBS regulations and Capstone culmination project standards; serve as the primary liaison between practicum faculty and the department. Contribute to program assessment, documentation, and accreditation-related reporting associated with clinical training. Engages in admissions process: reviews applications, interviews prospective students, and advises incoming students after acceptance. Teaching and Supervision Demonstrate excellence in teaching and a commitment to innovative, evidence-based pedagogical practices in graduate-level MFT courses, including practicum and/or supervision. Support students' integration of theory, research, and ethical practice within applied clinical settings. Contribute to the ongoing development of high-quality hybrid instruction. Advising Provide academic advisement and mentorship to 25 students with a focus on fostering academic, clinical, and professional development. Advise students regarding practicum readiness, site selection considerations, and licensure planning. Scholarship and Service Maintain an active program of scholarship consistent with CLT expectations. Participate in departmental, school, and university service. Attend bi-weekly Master's meetings; contribute to master's team problem-solving and supports master's program social events. Engage with professional and community organizations relevant to marriage and family therapy and clinical training. Position Annual Hiring Salary Range: $75,000 - $96,500 Hiring salary can be above the posted pay range if candidate's qualifications are determined to be above the minimum requirements of the position description. Requirements: Master's in Social Work (MSW), Marriage and Family Therapy (MFT), or Professional Clinical Counselor (PCC) or Doctorate (PhD, EdD, PsyD) in Marriage and Family Therapy or closely related discipline. Knowledge of California BBS regulations governing MFT trainees and associates. Experience in clinical supervision and/or practicum training. Preferred Qualifications Experience coordinating clinical placements in a graduate program. Familiarity with BBS accreditation and assessment processes. Experience in hybrid or online graduate education. Additional Information: Work Location : Doheny Campus (Downtown Los Angeles) Start Date: August 19, 2026 Applications Deadline: Open until filled Application Instructions: To Apply : Interested applicants should submit: A cover letter describing the applicant's fit with the specific position and university pillars of teaching Curriculum vitae or resume Teaching statement Course evaluations (un)official transcripts Two letters of reference via the Interview Exchange link Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questions: Please contact Dr. Paula Helu-Brown, Department of Psychology, phelu@msmu.edu Applicants must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the United States. The University will not assist applicants with any visa matters. A background check will be required. Employees may disclose their COVID-19 vaccination status with MSMU's Human Resources on a voluntary basis. Some MSMU clinical healthcare partners may require proof of COVID-19 vaccination to work at their facilities. If required, your academic division will inform you. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Chalon Campus, WEST LA 12001 Chalon Road Los Angeles, CA 90049 Doheny Campus, DOWNTOWN LA 10 Chester Place Los Angeles, CA 90007"
    },
    "https://msmu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205434": {
      "title": "Medical Director, Master of Physician Assistant Studies Program",
      "description": "Mount Saint Mary's University\nJob Posting: Medical Director, Master of Physician Assistant Studies Program Mount Saint Mary's University \n\tJob Posting: Medical Director, Master of Physician Assistant Studies Program Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Medical Director, Master of Physician Assistant Studies Program Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: Los Angeles, CA Posted: Oct 1, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 205434 Share Job Description: The Medical Director of the Master of Physician Assistant Studies (MPAS) Program at Mount Saint Mary's University serves as a clinical and professional resource to the Program Director, faculty, staff, and students and supports the development, implementation, and ongoing evaluation of the program. The Medical Director advocates for the Physician Assistant Program and actively participates in ensuring that the program's curriculum, competencies, and educational experiences reflect current standards of clinical practice and the contemporary role of the physician assistant. The Medical Director reports to the MPAS Program Director for activities directly related to the Physician Assistant Program and collaborates with program faculty and University leadership in support of the program's mission and accreditation requirements. Essential Duties and Responsibilities The Medical Director will: Actively participate in the development, review, and ongoing evaluation of the MPAS curriculum and program competencies to ensure alignment with current clinical practice standards and the role of the physician assistant. Serve as a clinical resource and advisor to the Program Director and program faculty regarding contemporary medical practice, patient care, healthcare delivery, and clinical education. Review relevant components of the didactic and clinical curriculum and provide recommendations regarding clinical accuracy, currency, scope, and appropriateness for entry-level PA practice. Participate in scheduled program faculty, curriculum, assessment, or other program meetings as appropriate to assigned responsibilities. Support the Program Director and faculty in evaluating the clinical relevance and effectiveness of the curriculum. Provide consultation regarding the development and evaluation of supervised clinical practice experiences and clinical education, as appropriate. Contribute to the development and review of program policies and procedures related to clinical education and patient care, as appropriate. Participate in program assessment, continuous quality improvement, and accreditation activities relevant to the Medical Director role. Participate in ARC-PA accreditation preparation and site visits and meet with accreditation representatives as requested. Serve as an advocate for the MPAS Program within the University, healthcare community, and clinical education community. Promote collaborative relationships between the MPAS Program, healthcare professionals, clinical partners, and the broader medical community. Participate in teaching, student assessment, clinical skills instruction, simulation, case-based learning, or other educational activities based upon expertise and program needs. Model professional, ethical, collaborative, patient-centered, and culturally responsive clinical practice. Perform other program-related responsibilities appropriate to the Medical Director role as assigned by the Program Director. Reports To: Program Director, Master of Physician Assistant Studies Program FTE: Part-time; FTE established by the University based upon assigned responsibilities (estimated .1-.2 FTEs, 4-8 hours/week) Position Annual Hiring Salary Range: $30,000-40,000 Hiring salary can be above the posted pay range if candidate's qualifications are determined to be above the minimum requirements of the position description. Appointment: Continuing appointment consistent with ARC-PA requirements Requirements: Required Qualifications The Medical Director must: Be a currently or previously licensed physician assistant, allopathic physician, or osteopathic physician. Be currently or previously board-certified in their profession or medical specialty, as applicable. Possess clinical experience and professional expertise appropriate to the educational needs of the MPAS Program. Demonstrate knowledge of contemporary clinical practice and the role of physician assistants within healthcare delivery. Demonstrate the ability to work collaboratively with faculty, administrators, clinicians, students, and external clinical partners. Demonstrate commitment to the mission and educational philosophy of Mount Saint Mary's University and the MPAS Program. Preferred Qualifications Current unrestricted professional licensure. Current board certification. Experience practicing collaboratively with physician assistants and/or other members of interprofessional healthcare teams. Experience in PA, medical, graduate health professions, or clinical education. Experience with curriculum development, competency-based education, student assessment, or clinical education. Familiarity with ARC-PA accreditation standards and processes. Experience serving diverse patient populations and communities. Accreditation Responsibilities The Medical Director is expected to maintain active participation in the MPAS Program consistent with applicable ARC-PA Standards. Participation includes supporting the development and routine review of the program curriculum and competencies and helping ensure that didactic and clinical education reflect current practice standards as they relate to the role of the physician assistant. The Medical Director will maintain sufficient involvement in program activities to demonstrate meaningful participation in fulfillment of the responsibilities of the position and will participate in accreditation-related activities and program review as required. Application Instructions: Application Procedure: Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Complete the online application and upload the following: vita cover letter describing the applicant's fit with the specific position (un)official transcripts two letters of reference. Questions: Please contact Dr. Jamal Bracken, MPA Program Director, JBRACKEN@msmu.edu Applicants must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the United States. The University will not assist applicants with any visa matters. A background check will be required. Employees may disclose their COVID-19 vaccination status with MSMU's Human Resources on a voluntary basis. Some MSMU clinical healthcare partners may require proof of COVID-19 vaccination to work at their facilities. If required, your academic division will inform you. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Chalon Campus, WEST LA 12001 Chalon Road Los Angeles, CA 90049 Doheny Campus, DOWNTOWN LA 10 Chester Place Los Angeles, CA 90007"
    },
    "https://msmu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203259": {
      "title": "Nursing Simulation / Skills Faculty, Assistant Professor, Full-time",
      "description": "Mount Saint Mary's University\nJob Posting: Nursing Simulation / Skills Faculty, Assistant Professor, Full-time Mount Saint Mary's University \n\tJob Posting: Nursing Simulation / Skills Faculty, Assistant Professor, Full-time Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Nursing Simulation / Skills Faculty, Assistant Professor, Full-time Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: Los Angeles, CA Posted: Jul 31, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Position ID: 203259 Share Job Description: The Department of Nursing is seeking a full-time assistant professor to serve as Simulation Educator across the nursing programs. This position includes teaching and participation in department and university governance. This position has a 21 unit teaching load with approximately 16 units assigned to simulation/skills and 5 units assigned to theory or clinical courses.  Duties include but are not limited to course lecturing and/or skills laboratory instruction; Sim coordination;  Scheduling; Technical operations of scenarios; Technical staff orientation and training; Simulation research; Liaison between departments.  This is a non-tenure-track faculty appointment (fall and spring semester) with a one-month summer assignment (10-month total appointment). Mount Saint Mary's University is home to the oldest Bachelor of Science in Nursing degree program in the State of California.  It is highly respected and enrolls the most students of any undergraduate program at the university.  The curriculum is based on the globally renowned Roy Adaptation Model, which was developed at MSMU by Sr. Callista Roy, CSJ. As a key member of a university founded by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, the TBSN Director is expected to embody and advance the CSJ charism -- service to the dear neighbor without distinction, commitment to justice, compassion, and inclusive community. This includes fostering a learning environment grounded in dignity, equity, and holistic care for students, faculty, and the communities we serve. To learn more about the TBSN program and the department's other nursing programs (which include a RN-BSN program, an accelerated BSN, a MSN, and newly launched DNP), visit: https://www.msmu.edu/departments/nursing/ . Position Annual Hiring Salary Range: $89,750.00 - $93,300.00 Hiring salary can be above the posted pay range if candidate's qualifications are determined to be above the minimum requirements of the position description. Requirements: An earned master's degree from a regionally accredited college or university. A clear and current California Registered Nurse license. California BRN approved to teach med/surg or eligible for approval. Two years of full-time experience in client care within the past 5 years. Familiarity with INACSL Standards of Best Practice and BRN simulation regulations. Ability to design, implement, and evaluate simulation scenarios and skills assessments. Flexibility in hours worked. Commitment to the university mission and the nursing department's philosophy. A proven track record of excellent teamwork, organization, and leadership skills. Preferred: One-year clinical teaching experience. Experience with high-fidelity manikins (Laerdal). Experience with LearningSpace AV platform. Experience in curriculum development and competency-based education. Experience training or supervising adjunct faculty. Application Instructions: Applicants must attach a cover letter,  and CV with California RN license number. Applicants must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the United States. The University will not assist applicants with any visa matters. A background check will be required. Employees may disclose their COVID-19 vaccination status with MSMU's Human Resources on a voluntary basis. Some MSMU clinical healthcare partners may require proof of COVID-19 vaccination to work at their facilities. If required, your academic division will inform you. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Chalon Campus, WEST LA 12001 Chalon Road Los Angeles, CA 90049 Doheny Campus, DOWNTOWN LA 10 Chester Place Los Angeles, CA 90007"
    },
    "https://msmu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=139867": {
      "title": "Part-Time Instructors for Anatomy and/or Physiology, Biological sciences Department",
      "description": "Mount Saint Mary's University\nJob Posting: Part-Time Instructors for Anatomy and/or Physiology, Biological sciences Department Mount Saint Mary's University \n\tJob Posting: Part-Time Instructors for Anatomy and/or Physiology, Biological sciences Department Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Part-Time Instructors for Anatomy and/or Physiology, Biological sciences Department Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Biological Sciences Locations: Los Angeles, CA Posted: Nov 24, 2021 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 139867 Share Job Description: These positions are filled on an as-needed basis, and recruitment is ongoing. We are seeking to attract and retain highly qualified faculty that share the University's and program's values. Anatomy and Physiology are required courses for the Bachelor's of Science in Nursing Degree Program at Mount Saint Mary's University, and as such, are part of Pre-Nursing Program. The curriculum and syllabus for these courses have been standardized across the institution in order to ensure a fair and robust learning experience for all students. The content of these courses were carefully selected to cover information that is vital to students to be successful in both the Nursing program as well as a future career in Nursing.  Most sections of these courses are in-person at one of our two campuses in Los Angeles. One campus, Chalon, is on the Westside of Los Angeles while Doheny is near downtown Los Angeles. Position Range: $2,092.50 per unit General Responsibilities Because Mount Saint Mary's Biology Department is committed to helping students achieve success in individual courses and in their Pre-Nursing track, we seek adjunct faculty members who are scholars as well as scholar-practitioners. The adjunct faculty member shall be responsible for the following: Teach assigned classes under the supervision of the Biology Department Chair and Pre-Nursing Program Director; Update a syllabus and course timeline based on the template each semester and post it online before class starts. Ensure that course content is in line with all the other sections of the course. Help students fulfill their maximum potential in mastering course content; Actively engage students through frequent interaction that motivates them to succeed and conveys a genuine energy and enthusiasm for their learning. Guide students through their studies using active collaboration and active learning techniques. Provide rich and regular constructive feedback, utilize rubrics effectively to assess student learning outcomes, and acknowledge student accomplishments. Maintain up-to-date grades on the online learning management system; Utilize current technology in the performance of job duties; Send student success alerts as needed to activate support systems for students who need extra help; Submit final grades in a timely fashion; Communicate with the Biology Department Chair and/or Pre-Nursing Program Director as necessary; Maintain a thorough and up-to-date subject-matter expertise; Maintain standards of professional conduct and ethics appropriate to the professional position; Abide by all relevant university and/or department procedures and policies. The above statements describe the job's essential responsibilities and requirements. They are not an exhaustive list of the duties that may be assigned to successful applicants. Requirements: Successful candidates should possess a Master's degree, Doctoral degree, or be a Doctoral candidate in the Biological Sciences, Nursing Practice, Physical Therapy, or a closely related field. The candidate will be able to teach undergraduate-level Anatomy and/or Physiology. The candidate will adhere to the common curriculum taught across all Anatomy and Physiology sections. The candidate will be able to integrate technology into the teaching and learning process. The candidate will be able to professionally interact with students, other educators, educational institution representatives, and the public. Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis. Please complete the online application and submit the following documents: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae - Your most recently updated CV Teaching accomplishments (examples include: course syllabus, course materials, course plans, teaching evaluations, etc.) (Un)official transcripts All materials should be sent via Interview Exchange Questions: Please contact the MSMU Biology Department to biology@msmu.edu Applicants must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the United States. The University will not assist applicants with any visa matters. A background check will be required. Employees may disclose their COVID-19 vaccination status with MSMU's Human Resources on a voluntary basis. Some MSMU clinical healthcare partners may require proof of COVID-19 vaccination to work at their facilities. If required, your academic division will inform you. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Chalon Campus, WEST LA 12001 Chalon Road Los Angeles, CA 90049 Doheny Campus, DOWNTOWN LA 10 Chester Place Los Angeles, CA 90007"
    },
    "https://msmu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=139866": {
      "title": "Part-Time Instructors for Microbiology",
      "description": "Mount Saint Mary's University\nJob Posting: Part-Time Instructors for Microbiology Mount Saint Mary's University \n\tJob Posting: Part-Time Instructors for Microbiology Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Part-Time Instructors for Microbiology Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Biological Sciences Locations: Los Angeles, CA Posted: Nov 24, 2021 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 139866 Share Job Description: These positions are filled on an as-needed basis, and recruitment is ongoing. We are seeking to attract and retain highly qualified faculty that share the University's and program's values. Microbiology is a required course for the Bachelor's of Science in Nursing Degree Program at Mount Saint Mary's University, and as such, are part of Pre-Nursing Program. The curriculum and syllabus for this course has been standardized across the institution in order to ensure a fair and robust learning experience for all students. The content of Microbiology has carefully selected to cover information that is vital to students to be successful in both the Nursing program as well as a future career in Nursing.  Most sections of this course are in-person at one of our two campuses in Los Angeles. One campus, Chalon, is on the Westside of Los Angeles while Doheny is near downtown Los Angeles. Position Range: $2,092.50 per unit General Responsibilities Because Mount Saint Mary's Biology Department is committed to helping students achieve success in individual courses and in their Pre-Nursing track, we seek adjunct faculty members who are scholars as well as scholar-practitioners. The adjunct faculty member shall be responsible for the following: Teach assigned classes under the supervision of the Biology Department Chair and Pre-Nursing Program Director; Update a syllabus and course timeline based on the template each semester and post it online before class starts. Ensure that course content is in line with all the other sections of the course. Help students fulfill their maximum potential in mastering course content; Actively engage students through frequent interaction that motivates them to succeed and conveys a genuine energy and enthusiasm for their learning. Guide students through their studies using active collaboration and active learning techniques. Provide rich and regular constructive feedback, utilize rubrics effectively to assess student learning outcomes, and acknowledge student accomplishments. Maintain up-to-date grades on the online learning management system; Utilize current technology in the performance of job duties; Send student success alerts as needed to activate support systems for students who need extra help; Submit final grades in a timely fashion; Communicate with the Biology Department Chair and Pre-Nursing Program Director as necessary; Maintain a thorough and up-to-date subject-matter expertise; Maintain standards of professional conduct and ethics appropriate to the professional position; Abide by all relevant university and/or department procedures and policies. The above statements describe the job's essential responsibilities and requirements. They are not an exhaustive list of the duties that may be assigned to successful applicants. Requirements: Successful candidates should possess a Master's degree or Doctoral degree or be a Doctoral candidate in the Biological Sciences, with demonstrated expertise in the field of Microbiology. The candidate will be able to teach undergraduate-level Microbiology. The candidate will adhere to the common curriculum taught across all Microbiology sections. The candidate will be able to integrate technology into the teaching and learning process. The candidate will be able to professionally interact with students, other educators, educational institution representatives, and the public. Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis. Please complete the online application and submit the following documents: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae - Your most recently updated CV Teaching accomplishments (examples include: course syllabus, course materials, course plans, teaching evaluations, etc.) (Un)official transcripts All materials should be sent via Interview Exchange Questions: Please contact the MSMU Biology Department to biology@msmu.edu Applicants must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the United States. The University will not assist applicants with any visa matters. A background check will be required. Employees may disclose their COVID-19 vaccination status with MSMU's Human Resources on a voluntary basis. Some MSMU clinical healthcare partners may require proof of COVID-19 vaccination to work at their facilities. If required, your academic division will inform you. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Chalon Campus, WEST LA 12001 Chalon Road Los Angeles, CA 90049 Doheny Campus, DOWNTOWN LA 10 Chester Place Los Angeles, CA 90007"
    },
    "https://msmu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=182210": {
      "title": "Part-Time Instructors for the History/Political Science Department",
      "description": "Mount Saint Mary's University\nJob Posting: Part-Time Instructors for the History/Political Science Department Mount Saint Mary's University \n\tJob Posting: Part-Time Instructors for the History/Political Science Department Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Part-Time Instructors for the History/Political Science Department Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: History/Political Science Locations: Los Angeles, CA Posted: Oct 17, 2024 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 182210 Share Job Description: General Responsibilities The adjunct faculty member shall be responsible for the following: teaching assigned classes under the supervision of the Chair of the Department of History and Political Science; helping students fulfill their maximum potential in mastering course content; assessing student learning outcomes; maintaining a thorough and up-to-date knowledge in the discipline; utilizing current technology in the performance of job duties; maintaining standards of professional conduct and ethics appropriate to the professional position; assisting with articulation and curriculum development and review. Requirements: Successful candidates should possess a Ph.D. or equivalent in History. The candidate will be able to teach both undergraduate and graduate level courses. Preferred Qualifications: Preference will be given to candidates with prior teaching experience A record of successfully advising, mentoring, or conducting research projects with students Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis. Please complete the online application and submit the following documents: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae - Your most recently updated CV Teaching accomplishments (examples include: course syllabus, course materials, course plans, teaching evaluations, etc.) (Un)official transcripts All materials should be sent via Interview Exchange Questions: Please contact the MSMU History/Political Science Department Chair, Lia Roberts at lroberts@msmu.edu Applicants must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the United States. The University will not assist applicants with any visa matters. A background check will be required. Employees may disclose their COVID-19 vaccination status with MSMU's Human Resources on a voluntary basis. Some MSMU clinical healthcare partners may require proof of COVID-19 vaccination to work at their facilities. If required, your academic division will inform you. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Chalon Campus, WEST LA 12001 Chalon Road Los Angeles, CA 90049 Doheny Campus, DOWNTOWN LA 10 Chester Place Los Angeles, CA 90007"
    }
